  "migrationRisks": [
    "BASE must become empty for the new root site. Adapt publisher, verifier, canonical URLs, JSON runtime/handoff fields, 404 and generated Home links together; root Home must not redirect to whatwhatboy.com.",
    "Critical: raw download URLs currently combine old WWB-HOST repository with build GITHUB_SHA. A new-repository SHA must point to the repository actually containing its artifact. Preserve old pinned raw/release URLs rather than silently changing them.",
    "Audit sender release API/allowlists, fixed trusted public-host metadata, new receiver job origin, popup fork/source links, host-file-entry.js and style-host-pages.cjs. The old uppercase /WWB-HOST/ URL returns404; /wwb-host/ currently returns200.",
    "Native guards already accept root /hosts/runtime paths. Preserve same-origin, exact firmware/path, trusted gesture, one-use ticket, reload/BFcache and durable uncertain-attempt locks. No global replacement in original native modules/BIN/ELF.",
    "The new domain shares origin with the current Pages project. Existing local/session storage persists. Never auto-clear old native attempt locks; reject obsolete path-bound receipts.",
    "Preserve 5 primary PS4 families and 3 disjoint PS5 families (builtin23+KARO subset6+ntfargo33=62 exact firmware versions). Preserve other original hosts as documented rather than inventing compatibility.",
    "Maintain 319 active native-file pins, original JS/BIN/ELF identities, cache closure, 38 public runtime JSON checks, native handoff JSON checks, shared/lazy catalogues, private-inventory exclusions and size budget.",
    "Browser automation was disabled in Work settings in this chat. Check available browser tools in the new chat. Do not bypass the restriction or invent screenshots. Visual previews and physical console operation must be reported honestly."
  ],
